Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-03-2001||09:41 PM||||Please let me apologize for this up front, but I insist it could not be helped . . .<P>There are about 1/4 million different stock Fiero steerings wheels distributed at the rate of roughly one per Fiero accross the surface of the Earth.<P>Now that it's done, I feel a lot better.<P>I think there are three types of steering wheels that came in the Fiero:  The good, the bad, and the ugly.<P>Or, early three spoke, the four spoke in later models, and the GT wheels which are a different three spoke from the early one<P>I have to wonder if the '88 Mera had a special wheel, it seems possible to me.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000002||theogre||03-04-2001||12:08 AM||||The 4 spoke paddle button wheels might not be the prettiest wheel on the planet but they are the most comfortable to drive with due to the thick rim. Those come in a soft plastic rim and a soft leather version.<P>||||reg||1
